# 🔌 Circuit – Hardware Configuration

This section documents the hardware components, pin assignments, and power connections used in the **Mimo Digital Pet** project.

## 1. Hardware Components

| S. No. | Component | Specification |
|---:|---|---|
| 1 | Microcontroller | ESP32 DevKit V1 |
| 2 | OLED Display | 1.3-inch SH1106, 128 × 64 |
| 3 | Touch Sensor | TTP223 Capacitive Touch Sensor |
| 4 | Servo Motor | SG90 Micro Servo |

## 2. Pin Configuration

| Component | Pin | ESP32 GPIO |
|---|---|---|
| OLED Display | SDA | GPIO 21 |
| OLED Display | SCL | GPIO 22 |
| Touch Sensor | OUT | GPIO 4 |
| Servo Motor | Signal | GPIO 18 |

## 3. Power Configuration

| Component | Power Supply |
|---|---|
| ESP32 | USB power |
| OLED Display | 3.3V from ESP32 |
| TTP223 Sensor | 3.3V from ESP32 |
| SG90 Servo | External regulated 5V supply |

**Common Ground:** The external servo power supply GND must be connected to the ESP32 GND.

## 4. Interface Details

- **I²C Communication:** The OLED display communicates with the ESP32 through the I²C interface.
- **Digital Input:** The TTP223 sensor sends touch detection signals to GPIO 4.
- **PWM Control:** The SG90 servo receives its control signal from GPIO 18.

## 5. Hardware Notes

- Verify pin connections before powering the system.
- Use a suitable regulated power supply for the servo motor.
- Ensure a common ground between the ESP32 and external servo supply.
- Avoid powering the servo directly from the ESP32 3.3V pin.
